Sackville ingests and indexes third-party documentation. Indexed content
remains under its own upstream license; Sackville records per-document
attribution in each index (the `attribution` column) and surfaces it in
results. The Apache-2.0 license above covers the Sackville software itself,
not the documentation it indexes.
